te":"2019-04-09T09:19:09-07:00","id":1303789,"title":"","content":"vampires as cultists? does that mean we could do the mummy as werewolf totem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T09:28:26-07:00","id":1303791,"title":"","content":"something like that, just a note that as of 2e they are trying to make mummy groups not just sorely mummies though their will be a mechanic to explain how that will happen given the nature of the Decent. Those without that mechanic can have their groups filled with Sekhmet Sorcerers and Immortals alongside the mummy player. I think thats how it goes anyway","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T11:59:04-07:00","id":1303809,"title":"","content":"I knew they were going to incorporate more varieties of immortals into Mummy 2e, I just didn't think anything more specific, like explicitly adding in the Purified, had been announced. It just seems really, really weird to add the Purified into Mummy because the game has double-downed so hard on what its mummy concept is that adding <i>another</i> mummy type that's unrelated to Irem would feel like theme dilution.<br /> <br /> It'd be like adding Inferno demons to the Demon the Descent core. Like, what are we trying to do here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T13:16:58-07:00","id":1303817,"title":"","content":"I dont think they ever said that specifically. More that the Arisen, who rose from the Rite of Return, are all from Irem and thus are Eygptian Mummies. Having the Purified in there shouldn't change it to much, because they aren't the central characters. Compared to mummies proper they are like wolf-blooded, like as it would be with the other Immortals. Their imperfect compared to the Deathless, which are the central focus here. All the other immortals are just side pieces one see in the perspective of playing mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T13:51:33-07:00","id":1303821,"title":"","content":"Seconding the recommendation for Second Sight: Third Eye, in my opinion it's a notable improvement on the ideas of first edition version despite not being an official product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member"